a16z-waymo:greenhouse:7774356.descriptionHtml:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#39;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver—The World&#39;s Most Experienced Driver™—to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;This role is at the intersection of robotics and machine learning, driving the next generation of operational efficiency for Waymo&#39;s rapidly expanding autonomous fleet. You will lead efforts to generalize complex depot operations—such as exterior cleaning, sensor calibration, and maintenance checks—using advanced robotics. Key work involves leveraging foundation models, reinforcement learning, simulation, and integrating ML models in production at scale. You will interface closely with operations teams to translate real-world needs into robust, working solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-root=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role follows a hybrid work schedule and reports to a Director, Hardware and Sensors.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive the next generation of operational efficiency for Waymo&#39;s rapidly expanding autonomous fleet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead efforts to generalize complex depot operations using advanced robotics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Focus on complex depot operations, such as exterior cleaning, sensor calibration, and maintenance checks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leverage foundation models, reinforcement learning, and simulation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate ML models in production at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interface closely with operations teams to translate real-world needs into robust, working solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 10 years of experience applying machine learning techniques to large-scale industrial problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in training and evaluating large machine learning models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in reinforcement learning and its applications to real-world problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prefer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PhD in Machine Learning, Robotics, or a related technical field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in robotics or embodied AI is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in collaborating with internal and external research partners on applying ML to large-scale industry scale problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The expected base salary range for this full-time position across US locations is listed below. Actual starting pay will be based on job-related factors, including exact work location, experience, relevant training and education, and skill level. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for the role location or, if the role can be performed remote, the specific salary range for your preferred location, during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Waymo employees are also eligible to participate in Waymo’s discretionary annual bonus program, equity incentive plan, and generous Company benefits program, subject to eligibility requirements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$298,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$368,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

a16z-waymo:greenhouse:7983686.descriptionHtml:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Waymo is an autonomous driving technology company with the mission to be the world&#39;s most trusted driver. Since its start as the Google Self-Driving Car Project in 2009, Waymo has focused on building the Waymo Driver—The World&#39;s Most Experienced Driver™—to improve access to mobility while saving thousands of lives now lost to traffic crashes. The Waymo Driver powers Waymo’s fully autonomous ride-hail service and can also be applied to a range of vehicle platforms and product use cases. The Waymo Driver has provided over ten million rider-only trips, enabled by its experience autonomously driving over 100 million miles on public roads and tens of billions in simulation across 15+ U.S. states.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;The Simulation Infrastructure team creates reliable, scalable, and cost-effective Simulation-based products that evaluate the Waymo Driver&#39;s software stack at a massive scale. We solve complex technical challenges to build services and tools for a broad range of customers Software Engineers, Product, Data Science, System Engineering, and more. So if you want to build the next generation of Simulation products and infrastructure, we&#39;d love to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This role follows a hybrid work schedule and reports to the Software Engineering Manager.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical leadership and people management for a team of software engineers building Waymo&#39;s distributed simulation engine&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect, scale, and operate the massive distributed system that validates the autonomous driving software stack daily&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive improvements in scheduler throughput, resource allocation, queuing latency, and cluster utilization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish team roadmaps, define engineering best practices, and mentor team members to support their technical growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with simulation, machine learning, and platform infrastructure teams to ensure seamless, high-throughput execution of their workloads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS or MS in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or equivalent field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of software engineering experience, with a proven track record of both technical leadership and people management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience designing, building, and operating large-scale distributed infrastructure or batch processing systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience optimizing large-scale job scheduling, resource orchestration, or queueing systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing or leading large scale systems and software development engineering teams&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We prefer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep experience with large-scale cluster management systems &amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong programming capabilities in Golang and C++&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of advanced operating systems, scheduling, containerization, sandboxing, or distributed file systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The expected base salary range for this full-time position across US locations is listed below. Actual starting pay will be based on job-related factors, including exact work location, experience, relevant training and education, and skill level. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for the role location or, if the role can be performed remote, the specific salary range for your preferred location, during the hiring process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Waymo employees are also eligible to participate in Waymo’s discretionary annual bonus program, equity incentive plan, and generous Company benefits program, subject to eligibility requirements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$251,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$310,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

a16z-zipline:greenhouse:7510960003.descriptionHtml:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Zipline&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zipline is the world’s largest and most experienced drone delivery service. We are on a mission to serve all humans equally by ensuring access to food, medicine and essential goods anytime, anywhere. We design, build, and operate the world’s largest autonomous logistics system, delivering critical supplies quickly and reliably. Today, Zipline operates on four continents, makes a delivery somewhere in the world every 30 seconds, and has completed millions of deliveries to date, including blood, vaccines, medical supplies, food, and retail products.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our customers include the world’s largest and most prominent healthcare systems, governments, retailers, restaurants and global businesses who rely on us to save lives, reduce emissions, increase economic opportunity, and provide delivery from point A to point B as fast as possible. The drone is only 15% of what we’ve built to enable seamless, reliable, global operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our system strengthens supply chains, reduces congestion, and gives people time back. With more than 140 million commercial autonomous miles safely flown, Zipline is redefining access to healthcare, consumer products, and food across the globe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We operate at a global scale and are looking for practical problem solvers who thrive on real-world challenges and rapid growth. Our team is motivated by building systems that have a direct, meaningful impact on people’s lives and by scaling the future of logistics. We are seeking people who sculpt from first principles, enjoy facing adversity, and can do the impossible at record breaking speeds.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You and The Role&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be working with our latest prototype avionics, powertrain and mechanisms and collaborating with engineers on design iterations as well as supporting field operations to maintain our flight vehicles. You will be responsible for running tests from quick semi-automated vehicle check-outs all the way to long reliability and endurance campaigns, all with clearly documented results. And lastly you will build large jigs and structures to support full system vehicle testing and development, think wind cannons, tether mounts, and barriers for safety.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;content&quot;&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build up vehicle components and test jigs using instructions ranging in quality / completeness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Replace vehicle parts following instructions and updating documentation in the process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Verify that test specifications are correct and can be executed on given resources available.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create test setups to match engineering specifications which includes interpretation of test procedures and diagrams, instrumentation, data acquisition, test article diagnostics and front line root causing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write high quality and detailed reports that drive to the root of any issues on a given test using data and a first order analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;section-wrapper page-full-width&quot;&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a machine shop and operating common mechanical equipment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with electronics at different power levels and component size&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on hardware/software projects and collaborating with hardware engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working on hardware/software projects and collaborating with hardware engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to understand and interpret a wide variety of technical documents (electrical specification, mechanical drawings, etc…)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to organize data in a way that is easy to understand&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work rotating shifts, including nights and weekends&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 class=&quot;content-wrapper posting-page&quot;&gt;What Else You Need to Know&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;The starting cash range for this role is $32 - $42/ hour. Please note that this is a target, starting cash range for a candidate who meets the minimum qualifications for this role. The final cash pay for this role will depend on a variety of factors, including a specific candidate&#39;s experience, qualifications, skills, working location, and projected impact. The total compensation package for this role may also include: equity compensation; overtime pay; discretionary annual or performance bonuses; sales incentives; benefits such as medical, dental and vision insurance; paid time off; and more.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Zipline is an equal opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, ancestry, national origin, religion or religious creed, mental or physical disability, medical condition, genetic information, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital status, military or veteran status, citizenship, or other characteristics protected by state, federal or local law or our other policies.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;We value diversity at Zipline and welcome applications from those who are traditionally underrepresented in tech. If you like the sound of this position but are not sure if you are the perfect fit, please apply!&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

a16z-zipline:greenhouse:7623149003.descriptionHtml:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;About Zipline&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zipline is the world’s largest and most experienced drone delivery service. We are on a mission to serve all humans equally by ensuring access to food, medicine and essential goods anytime, anywhere. We design, build, and operate the world’s largest autonomous logistics system, delivering critical supplies quickly and reliably. Today, Zipline operates on four continents, makes a delivery somewhere in the world every 30 seconds, and has completed millions of deliveries to date, including blood, vaccines, medical supplies, food, and retail products.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our customers include the world’s largest and most prominent healthcare systems, governments, retailers, restaurants and global businesses who rely on us to save lives, reduce emissions, increase economic opportunity, and provide delivery from point A to point B as fast as possible. The drone is only 15% of what we’ve built to enable seamless, reliable, global operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our system strengthens supply chains, reduces congestion, and gives people time back. With more than 140 million commercial autonomous miles safely flown, Zipline is redefining access to healthcare, consumer products, and food across the globe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We operate at a global scale and are looking for practical problem solvers who thrive on real-world challenges and rapid growth. Our team is motivated by building systems that have a direct, meaningful impact on people’s lives and by scaling the future of logistics. We are seeking people who sculpt from first principles, enjoy facing adversity, and can do the impossible at record breaking speeds.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About the Role&lt;/h3&gt;
As Head of Strategic Finance, Africa, you will be a senior leader on Zipline’s Strategic Finance team and a core member of Zipline’s Africa Leadership Team. You will have end-to-end responsibility for financial strategy, planning, and performance management for Zipline’s Africa business, while playing a critical role in shaping Zipline’s global, consolidated financial strategy.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Global Head of Strategic Finance, this role sits at the intersection of enterprise-wide decision-making and regional execution. Strategic Finance at Zipline owns the company’s consolidated business model, long-range planning, capital allocation, and global financial strategy – this role is a key leader within that function. You will ensure Africa strategy, investments, and performance are tightly integrated into Zipline’s overall business plan.&lt;/p&gt;
As a member of the Africa Leadership Team, you will serve as a trusted financial partner to regional leadership, supporting operational execution, growth initiatives, and partnerships across multiple African markets.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role also carries responsibility for building a small, high-impact team. Your team will provide direct, embedded partnership to leaders across Africa’s Go-to-Market, Engineering, Operations, and G&amp;amp;A functions. Driving financial literacy across the organization so teams understand unit economics, tradeoffs, and long-term implications of their decisions is critical to Zipline Africa’s success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;This is an in-person role based in South San Francisco, CA&lt;/strong&gt;, where Zipline’s Strategic Finance team and many of our go-to-market, operations, and engineering partners are located. The role includes periodic travel to Africa to work closely with in-country operators and to engage with key government, donor, and commercial partners.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;strong&gt;Global &amp;amp; Regional Financial Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own financial strategy, planning, and performance management for Zipline’s Africa business as part of the company’s global consolidated business, reporting into the Global Head of Strategic Finance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a strategic advisor to Zipline’s Africa leadership on investment decisions, growth strategy, unit economics, and long-term sustainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute directly to Zipline’s enterprise-level strategy, long-range planning, and capital allocation decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain long-term financial models to evaluate market strategies, expansion plans, and new business initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Planning, Forecasting &amp;amp; Performance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead budgeting, forecasting, and performance analysis for Africa operations within Zipline’s global planning framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to improve efficiency, profitability, and capital effectiveness while maintaining operational excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex operational and commercial dynamics into clear, actionable financial insights for executive and regional leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Finance &amp;amp; Business Partnering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a financial thought partner to Africa operations leadership, helping teams navigate financial complexity while driving sustainable growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Go-to-Market, Engineering, Operations, Supply Chain, Deployment, and G&amp;amp;A teams to support cost-effective execution and strong unit economics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with government, donor, and commercial partners to structure financially viable contracts and long-term partnerships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership &amp;amp; Strategic Enablement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a small, high-caliber team to manage Zipline’s Africa business model.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide direct, embedded partnership to GTM, Engineering, Ops, and G&amp;amp;A teams to guide strategic choices and investment decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive financial literacy across the organization, ensuring leaders and teams understand unit economics, tradeoffs, and long-term financial implications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish finance as an enabling function that helps teams move faster and make better decisions while balancing growth and sustainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set a high bar for analytical rigor, clarity of communication, and business judgment across the Strategic Finance team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accounting, Compliance &amp;amp; Controls&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with regional finance and accounting teams to ensure accurate financial reporting, efficient close processes, and strong internal controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with US-based finance leadership to standardize financial practices across global operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support audits and regulatory engagements; coordinate with local and US-based tax advisors to ensure compliance across African entities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scaling Zipline’s Platforms&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead financial analysis to support the scalability and profitability of Zipline’s Platform 1 operations in Africa.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate pricing strategies, market expansion opportunities, and operational tradeoffs to drive sustainable growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally to assess the financial feasibility of launching new products and services, including Platform 2, in Africa.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in finance, including 5+ years in a senior or leadership role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting or leading finance for a high-growth, operations-intensive business (e.g., logistics, supply chain, manufacturing, infrastructure).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong financial modeling, forecasting, and strategic analysis skills, with the ability to operate at both detailed and enterprise levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with international or regional finance teams; exposure to African markets is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with governments as clients or partners, including structuring, pricing, or supporting complex public-sector engagements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with the U.S. government (e.g., federal agencies, state or local governments, or U.S.-based public-sector programs) is a strong plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of IFRS and familiarity with multi-entity, multi-currency environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience building and leading small, high-performing teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate complex financial concepts into clear, actionable guidance for non-finance partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive presence, communication skills, and comfort operating in fast-paced, ambiguous environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating in a matrixed leadership environment, balancing enterprise ownership with regional leadership responsibilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What Else You Need to Know&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The starting cash range for this role is $220,000-$250,000, plus equity for candidates based in San Francisco, CA. Please note that this is a target, starting cash range for a candidate who meets the minimum qualifications for this role. The final cash pay for this role will depend on a variety of factors, including a specific candidate&#39;s experience, qualifications, skills, working location, and projected impact. The total compensation package for this role may also include: discretionary annual or performance bonuses; sales incentives; benefits such as medical, dental and vision insurance; paid time off; and more.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Zipline is an equal opportunity employer and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, ancestry, national origin, religion or religious creed, mental or physical disability, medical condition, genetic information, sex (including pregnancy, childbirth, and related medical conditions), sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, age, marital status, military or veteran status, citizenship, or other characteristics protected by state, federal or local law or our other policies.&lt;/p&gt;
We value diversity at Zipline and welcome applications from those who are traditionally underrepresented in tech. If you like the sound of this position but are not sure if you are the perfect fit, please apply!&lt;/div&gt;

alphapartners-coupang:greenhouse:7518366.descriptionHtml:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Fire Safety Manager&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Description&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Fire Safety &amp;amp; Compliance Management &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Fire Safety &amp;amp; Compliance Management Develop, implement, and enforce fire safety policies and procedures in compliance with Taiwan&#39;s fire codes and regulations. Conduct fire risk assessments, safety inspections, and audits to identify potential hazards and recommend mitigation strategies. Collaborate with regulatory agencies, authorities having jurisdiction (AHJs), and fire departments to ensure compliance with fire safety laws. Lead fire protection system inspections, maintenance, and performance evaluations to ensure optimal functionality.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Fire Prevention &amp;amp; Risk Mitigation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Fire Prevention &amp;amp; Risk Mitigation Establish and execute fire prevention programs, ensuring best practices are adopted across all facilities. Oversee the design, installation, and maintenance of fire detection, alarm, and suppression systems. Implement hot work permit programs, fire drills, and evacuation plans to ensure operational readiness. Develop and maintain fire load assessments to evaluate and minimize potential fire risks.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Emergency Response &amp;amp; Crisis Management&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Emergency Response &amp;amp; Crisis Management Lead the development of fire emergency response plans and conduct regular fire drills. Train employees and emergency response teams on fire safety procedures, evacuation protocols, and fire extinguisher use. Act as a liaison with local emergency services to coordinate emergency response efforts effectively. Develop business continuity strategies related to fire incidents to minimize disruptions and ensure swift recovery.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Fire Safety Training &amp;amp; Awareness&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Fire Safety Training &amp;amp; Awareness Design and deliver fire safety training programs for employees, contractors, and facility teams. Ensure all personnel are equipped with knowledge of fire prevention and practices and emergency response protocols. Foster a strong fire safety culture through awareness campaigns and engagement initiatives.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Data Management &amp;amp; Reporting&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Data Management &amp;amp; Reporting Maintain comprehensive records of fire incidents, safety inspections, and compliance reports. Analyze fire safety data to identify trends and drive continuous improvement initiatives. Provide executive-level reports and recommendations on fire safety performance and risk reduction strategies.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Qualifications Required: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Fire Safety, Fire Science, Engineering, or a related field.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Minimum of 8 years of fire prevention experience, preferably in a corporate, industrial, or authority having jurisdiction (AHJ) setting.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Strong knowledge of Taiwan&#39;s fire safety regulations, NFPA standards, and global fire codes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Experience in fire risk assessment, compliance audits, and emergency planning.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Proficiency in fire protection system design, maintenance, and evaluation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Excellent leadership, problem solving, and stakeholder management skills.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Preferred: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Advanced degree in Fire Science, Engineering or Occupational Safety.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Certifications such as Certified Fire Protection Specialist (CFPS), NFPA, or equivalent.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Experience with fire safety technology, AI-enabled fire monitoring, and digital compliance tracking.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Bilingual proficiency in Mandarin and English.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Prior experience in multinational corporations or high-risk operational environments.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Privacy Notice​&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233279&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134245417&amp;quot;:false}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li data-leveltext=&quot;&quot; data-font=&quot;Symbol&quot; data-listid=&quot;31&quot; data-list-defn-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335552541&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;335559685&amp;quot;:720,&amp;quot;335559991&amp;quot;:360,&amp;quot;469769226&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Symbol&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469769242&amp;quot;:[8226],&amp;quot;469777803&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;left&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777804&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;469777815&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;multilevel&amp;quot;}&quot; data-aria-posinset=&quot;1&quot; data-aria-level=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Your personal information will be collected and managed by Coupang as stated in the Application Privacy Notice located below:&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.coupang.jobs/privacy-policy/&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-charstyle=&quot;Hyperlink&quot;&gt;https://www.coupang.jobs/privacy-policy/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;​&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233279&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134245417&amp;quot;:false}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
